From 9b73dd7893a255af60daf01f0489280119fe0ab5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:32:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Track FX: NEON volume/pan/reverb send,
 phaser/chorus/flanger/EQ/SRR loops with state in registers (bit-exact)

Bit-exact: every call gives the same output for the same input. New track_fx_kernels.h holds the loops.

- processReverbSendAndVolume: 4 samples at a time with NEON (vld2/vst2), one loop per case (reverb send on/off,
  into the mix or in place). smmul on 4 lanes = 2 x vmull.s32 + vuzp (the high words of the exact 64-bit products,
  no saturation case; vqdmulh would saturate INT32_MIN * INT32_MIN). The volume ramp is vol + k * inc mod 2^32,
  the same added 1 or 4 steps at a time; without doAmplitudeIncrement inc = 0 (the old unused pan scaling of an
  uninitialised increment is gone). All adds wrap as the old ARM add did (NEON adds, scalar in uint32_t). The
  buffer, the mix and the engine's reverb buffer are separate arrays; in place each sample is read before written.
  The last 0-3 samples run scalar. The double division for the ramp is unchanged (vdiv.f64).
- processFX: phaser, chorus, stereo chorus and flanger each in their own loop, with LFO, write index and the
  phaser/allpass memories in locals, stored back after (the old loop kept them in the object, which every store to
  the buffer forced out and back; the buffer never lies in the object). Per sample the same operations in the same
  order. Phaser: the coefficients a1/-a1 come from the LFO alone, so they are worked out for 32 samples first; L and
  R then run separately (they share nothing but a1), smmulr kept in program order by a volatile asm (same
  instruction) so the 7 state values fit in registers. -a1 cannot overflow (a1 in 1..2^31-1). Grain keeps the
  old loop (unchanged body). EQ: doEQ per sample became eq<bass, treble> with the filter states in locals.
- processSRRAndBitcrushing: SRR loop unchanged but with its state in locals; bitcrush alone ANDs 4 samples at a
  time with NEON (same mask per int32).

Proof: tests/bench/effects (ARM=1, firmware code in the Cortex-A9 emulator): 18 fixed cases plus 4 x 4000 random
cases (parameters changing between blocks, 1-128 samples incl. odd, mono/stereo, silence, full scale, extremes,
random start states), all hashes the same as v12-perf. Song: tests/bench/effects/song_trace.sh with
EMU_OPTS="--init-sounds --seed 1": all 165,312 calls (55,104 each) identical, measured.wav identical.

Demand (tests/song, per 128 samples): 1,095,537 -> 1,035,101 (-5.5 %): processReverbSendAndVolume 59,412 ->
13,977, processFX 38,643 -> 24,040, processSRRAndBitcrushing 5,397 -> 5,014. Device run: voices 28.5 -> 31.9.
Code +2,510 bytes; stack: processFX +320 bytes (phaser coefficients), processReverbSendAndVolume +120,
processSRRAndBitcrushing +24.

Not changed: the compressor. Its render() float math is compiled with -funsafe-math-optimizations and the
compiler picks NEON reciprocal estimates or VFP divisions by context; a loop change made the random test differ.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
